(119, 81, 'directions', 'Kelly Dahl Campground is located between Central City and Nederland on CO119. Kelly Dahl is a Forest Service campground, noted on the map as (P)10. During the fall and spring, Kelly Dahl isn’t used very much. During the winter months, it is normally cabled. There are tables and restrooms, bring your water during the off-season. </br>\r\n<b>Note:</br> Check with the Roosevelt National Forest Office about the intent of the cable and winter use.</br>\r\n<b>How to Get there:</b> The easiest way to get to Kelly Dahl is by taking your favorite highway to the city of Boulder. Drive up Boulder Canyon (CO119) west to Nederland. Take CO119 south for 3 miles: Kelly Dahl CG is on the east side of CO119 just after the intersection with\r\nCO72. </br>', 'Kelly Dahl Campground is located between Central City and Nederland on CO119. Kelly Dahl is a Forest Service campground, noted on the map as (P)10. During the fall and spring, Kelly Dahl isn’t used very much. During the winter months, it is normally cabled. There are tables and restrooms, bring your water during the off-season. </br>\r\n<b>Note:</b> Check with the Roosevelt National Forest Office about the intent of the cable and winter use.</br>\r\n<b>How to Get there:</b> The easiest way to get to Kelly Dahl is by taking your favorite highway to the city of Boulder. Drive up Boulder Canyon (CO119) west to Nederland. Take CO119 south for 3 miles: Kelly Dahl CG is on the east side of CO119 just after the intersection with\r\nCO72. </br>', 'rhall290472', '2024-09-14 01:28:11'),
